{"kind":"request","text":"Stop disclosing live session identifiers, and state the loopback trust boundary where sessions are documented.","body":{"conditions":"GET /v0/presence returns the presence map keyed by raw session identifiers (Hub.Snapshot copies presence[id]), and POST /v0/presence accepts any local claim of any custodial actor name with no proof — so within loopback, one client can read another session's identifier and then speak and act as that session's actor through /v0/say and /v0/act, breaking the stated invariant that a session speaks only as its bound actor. The multi-actor custodian posture accepts local trust, but the session-identifier disclosure is gratuitous: key presence responses by display identity, not by session; require the announcing client to prove or freshly mint its session rather than adopt an observed one; add a test that one session cannot address another's lease; and state the remaining loopback trust boundary plainly in docs/reference.md. Obtain independent exact-head review before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}